SplitPhaseSemanticSubmissionResult

#### submitPartitionSemanticResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Complete an issued partition semantic task using SplitPhasePartitionSemanticResult
and the exact common CNCF completion envelope. Enriched supplies only the ordered
unknown estimates and semantic boundary judgments requested by Workflow;
DecisionNeeded is semantic data, not Human consent. Workflow validates coverage,
evidence, original actor/context and native suspension before canonical completion.
It owns calibration, enumeration, packing and ranking. The returned acknowledgement
does not prove downstream planning or document application; use the assigned
completion route rather than a client-selected admission operation.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhasePartitionSemanticResult

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseSemanticSubmissionResult

#### advanceSplitPhase

##### DESCRIPTION

Observe the selected native instance and original context from SplitPhaseAdvanceCommand; there is no caller-selected stage or candidate. Workflow absorbs available mechanical work and returns the genuine next semantic task, retained observation or actual failure. The normal paired Human connection issues genuine scope/reasoning Decisions and continues independently verified ProvideResolution or records Defer/Cancel. ALL-Built must not be converted into a Human task. The saved Start mode determines complete Preview or authorized managed Apply. Document-conflict semantic/Human handlers remain unavailable; unavailable capability is not a successful WAIT or Terminal. Integrated regression/review and proof of full split success remain unfinished.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseAdvanceCommand

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseAdvanceResult

#### submitHandoffScopeResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Complete the exact issued handoff task with SplitPhaseScopeSemanticResult in
the common CNCF result envelope. Enriched supplies nonempty ordered subsets of
the original producing/receiving ranges for exactly the issued gaps; DecisionNeeded
supplies no partial scopes. Evidence must match the actual execution, actor,
checkpoint and native suspension. Canonical completion acknowledges this semantic
boundary only. It preserves the entire candidate frontier, ownership, closure
and transfer authority; it does not select downstream operations or apply documents.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseScopeSemanticResult

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseScopeSubmissionResult

#### submitReasoningResult

##### DESCRIPTION

Complete the exact issued reasoning classification task using SplitPhaseReasoningSemanticResult in the common CNCF result envelope. Return only the ordered unknown-item classifications, rationale and evidence, or DecisionNeeded without partial assignments. The common result reference must equal the result identity/revision assigned in the request for either alternative; the participant cannot select another destination. Workflow owns admission, replacement data references and objective-only continuation over the original frontier. The normal v12 paired composition installs native reasoning completion and retained successor observation. A completion acknowledgement is not Preview, Apply or integrated acceptance, nor permission to select a stage or command.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseReasoningSemanticResult

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseReasoningSubmissionResult

#### submitSplitHumanDirection

##### DESCRIPTION

Complete the exact issued Human Decision with the common CNCF result envelope containing SplitPhaseHumanDirectionAnswer. The paired host assembly requires an independent verifier bound to the complete question/result and current owning call; an authenticated relay alone is not consent. ProvideResolution names separate interpretation data, while Defer and Cancel carry no resolution. The normal paired composition supports separately verified scope and reasoning answers. Scope completion saves HumanAnswered; later advance observes resolution data and continues planning/reasoning, or appends Defer/Cancel termination. Reasoning completion atomically saves its answer and selected successor or stopped state; later advance observes the saved Preview or Terminal. An answer acknowledgement is not that outcome or document application. Document-conflict semantic/Human resolution is not installed. Identical retained answers are observations, not new consent; changed answers or uncertain commits must not be auto-replayed.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseHumanDirectionAnswer

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

SplitPhaseHumanDirectionSubmissionResult

# SERVICE

## RepositoryHumanService

### DESCRIPTION

Independent Human channel for a retained RepositorySync semantic conflict that
could not be decided. Present the original base/local/remote text and rationale;
do not infer consent from AI output or login identity. Only the exact issued
Decision completion may return the Human answer. This declaration installs no
channel, command executor or source/remote permission.

### OPERATION

#### presentRepositoryConflictDecision

##### DESCRIPTION

Present only the exact Workflow-issued conflict question, including its original
texts and rationale, through the independent Human channel. Return the declared
answer through the assigned completion route; do not substitute an AI judgment
or infer consent from login identity. Workflow verifies the answer and owns later
resolution effects. This operation performs no file, Git or synchronization effect.

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncHumanConflictRequest

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

RepositorySyncHumanConflictAnswer

